+//! Issue #681 (slice 4b of 7 of the #635 re-slicing, 0016 decision 7(e)): **the three
+//! maintenance passes that walk the committed namespace themselves — reconstruction, backfill,
+//! rebalance — resolve every committed object the way every other consumer resolves one, contain
+//! per object what they cannot read, and refuse (rather than abort or silently discard) the work
+//! this slice does not own.**
+//!
+//! On the base all three read the chunk map inline out of the inode record
+//! (`record.chunk_map.as_flat().ok_or(SegmentedMapUnsupported)?`, seven sites), so ONE segmented
+//! object turns repair, fill and drain into an `Err` for EVERY object in the store — and these
+//! are the passes that *restore redundancy*. A record that will not `decode` ends the walk the
+//! same way, before any resolver is involved.
+//!
+//! Six legs, each driving ALL THREE passes over ONE store — one test per property, never one per
+//! pass. Four pinned decisions ride as sub-assertions of an existing leg rather than as legs of
+//! their own: leg 3 carries "an empty queue certifies over the reading it never made" and "a
+//! record is read, written and named under exactly the key the store gave it", leg 2 carries
+//! "one refusal line per object", leg 6 carries "attribution before the work".
+//!
+//! **No assertion here names the answer's new shape:** the production files are reverted under
+//! the per-fix red leg, so naming a symbol this patch introduces would make that leg fail to
+//! COMPILE and the red would degrade to "a symbol is missing". Every leg is expressed in
+//! base-visible entries only — `Reconciled::Blocked` exists on the base (`reconciliation.rs:44`).
+
